; a `forall` premise is searched with a fresh variable for its bound variable, which stands for
; an arbitrary object: no variable of the rule may take a value containing it. Before, `$T`
; below could become `v ^ 1` (for the fresh `v`), since `v = v ^ 1` holds by the first axiom --
; so `$T` depended on `$x` after all, and `Q` followed, although "some term equals every x"
; only holds in a domain with a single element
load equality
bool Q
use $a ^ 1 = $a
use (forall $x ($x = $T)) implies Q    "attack"
expect "ProofError"
    Q
